<title>USA: Petro Stopping Centers sells $135 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Petro Stopping Centers sells $135 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a high-yield debt offering from Petro Stopping Centers was priced on Thursday by lead manager, CIBC Wood Gundy Securities Inc, according to market sources.</p>
<p>BORROWER PETRO STOPPING CENTERS INC</p>
<p>AMT $135 MLN	 COUPON 10.5 PCT   MATURITY 2/01/07</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 100     FIRST PAY DATE 7/1/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B3    YIELD 10.5 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B	   SPREAD 396 BPS    CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE FOR</p>
<p>							    FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>NOTES: Three-year equity call for 35 percent of issue at 110.5. The size of the deal was increased to $135 million from an original amount of $125 million.</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1662</p>
</text>
